6. ANSWER

FINAL ONE-LINE ANSWER: the '51-100' patients_seen group - severe COVID-19 in BCG 3/15 vs placebo 0/22 (chi-square p=0.0287, Fisher p=0.0586, Yates p=0.1153, Holm-adjusted chi-square p=0.0860); it is the ONLY band with unadjusted chi-square p<0.05 ('1-50': chi2 p=0.1036, '>100': chi2 p=1.0000); gate used = the unadjusted chi-square p<0.05 the question asks for, finding is fragile (NOT significant after Holm adjustment (Holm p=0.0860), but Fisher exact p=0.0586 is NOT <0.05 and min expected count=1.22<5, so the exact test governs, and significant in only 2/6 severity definitions); caveat: 'COVID-19 severity' is a data-derived inference (worst AEHS>=3 among COVID-19 AE records; AEHS 0-7, 7=death) because no CRD/protocol/CRF is supplied with the capsule.
STABILITY VERDICT: A single band ('51-100') is ever significant, but significance is NOT stable across severity definitions (2/6); report it with the definition attached, not as a robust effect.
